Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:07:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER: VS Code designer view for the web HMI pages
 (click a component -> DFM properties + events, double-click an event -> its
 code)

tools/vscode-htdesigner: a plain-JS VS Code extension (no npm needed).
- the page renders in a webview behind a no-network CSP (no ws:/http:, no frames,
  no form posts), so a preview can never reach wb_gateway / wb_serve; in design
  mode the page's own click handlers do not run
- the in-page probe records every listener the page binds (with the call stack),
  so "which JS handles this button" is measured, not guessed
- an event opens its code in one of three places: the web JS listener, the C++
  port (TfXxx::Handler, #if 0 / comment-mention aware), or the BCB6 original
  (Big5, served through a read-only file system -- cannot be saved back as UTF-8)
- read-only: writes no file

Tests (all read-only, scratch in %TEMP%): test\run_all.ps1 [-WithVSCode]
  lib 33 / probe in headless Edge 2 pages / extension with fake vscode 23 /
  real VS Code 1.139 incl. an 8-page sweep 34 -- all pass; the page's own
  ws://.../ht9045 attempts were blocked on 5 of the swept pages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
